nt_uuid":"08d2ac68-180a-451a-8b16-b8db1309d84a","position":{"commit_sha":"88040e78f3f48229c5a7da6c8016bc68d885917a","position":"1787907842254130400-08d2ac68-180a-451a-8b16-b8db1309d84a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"a84fdeae99ff6814d837e7616ce155fc052f73aa82741135847fd424242454db","event_uuid":"b9b9adb4-26c2-41e1-9a5c-7eb55ecd5e30","position":{"commit_sha":"199497f39184565bf1f6de6e929edcfa2f8a67ce","position":"1787908595135531941-b9b9adb4-26c2-41e1-9a5c-7eb55ecd5e30"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"b0f0d0a198ef97dd06b6ae799b155f7cc9bdc87ea7a3801338bf8aa076360e96","event_uuid":"f4f75336-618d-4b1b-b8f4-1078460487cf","position":{"commit_sha":"ef622d15683f60d85727cbabefc22fff0d36035a","position":"1787909106783019001-f4f75336-618d-4b1b-b8f4-1078460487cf"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"883fad12ea10eb4cd29907cf65baca7102bfd865918e82f110b1eb21a21afcd0","event_uuid":"8c5e2aec-e139-45b4-bde1-080234655011","position":{"commit_sha":"d74b059dc0c9ece92e31d04fb8a1c44b875424ed","position":"1787909826664948815-8c5e2aec-e139-45b4-bde1-080234655011"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787866557605990730,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"749fd85f-b14b-468a-96a0-d002c60c063a","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"0804-9a6b-9182-42c9"},{"link_uuid":"7e4fb90c-f4cd-4d9a-b5b7-8f93a449e819","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"dab7-cfa3-a860-4678"},{"link_uuid":"5a327ba8-77d8-4482-9ad0-df1b6fcbdb81","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"53b7-951c-df4b-4e36"},{"link_uuid":"08d2ac68-180a-451a-8b16-b8db1309d84a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"954a-6596-6de9-47a3"},{"link_uuid":"b9b9adb4-26c2-41e1-9a5c-7eb55ecd5e30","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"3c0d-802b-e17c-4b91"},{"link_uuid":"8c5e2aec-e139-45b4-bde1-080234655011","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"72b9-9a83-d4d5-4ea3"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`import rebar` callers get a return value, not a terminal, so the first-class way to raise a\nnon-fatal warning is Python's **`warnings`** subsystem (not `logging`, which the brainstorm\nrejected). This story emits a `warnings.warn` of a dedicated category from single-ticket\nlibrary functions when the detector fires. Depends on the merged detector\n(`cross_session_warning_for`) and reducer clearing: a ticket not `in_progress` has no\nholder, so the detector returns `None` and nothing is emitted.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd a new module `src/rebar/_lib_warn.py` defining `class CrossSessionWarning(UserWarning)`\nand a best-effort helper `emit_cross_session_warning(ticket_id, *, repo_root=None)`;\nre-export the category as `rebar.CrossSessionWarning` so callers can filter/escalate it with\nstdlib filters. The module also exposes a `suppress_cross_session_warning()` context manager\n(holds the same guard) so an outer surface that already advises stops the library channel\nfrom doubling it (see Surface layering).\n\nThe helper mirrors the CLI's `_maybe_warn_cross_session`: it calls the merged detector\n`cross_session_warning_for(ticket_id, repo_root=repo_root)` and, on a non-`None` string,\ncalls `warnings.warn(msg, CrossSessionWarning)`; on `None` it does nothing. Two properties matter:\n\n- **Best-effort — never breaks the call.** The whole body is wrapped in\n  `try/except Exception: pass`; the library operation always proceeds and no warning is emitted on failure.\n- **Re-entrancy-guarded.** The merged detector (`src/rebar/_commands/cross_session.py`)\n  itself calls public `rebar._lib_reads.show_ticket`, so a naive emit on `show_ticket` would\n  recurse. A module-level `contextvars.ContextVar` (`_EMITTING`, default `False`) makes the\n  helper a no-op while an emit is in progress (returns if set, else sets it, runs, resets in\n  `finally`), so the detector's internal read emits nothing and exactly one warning fires per\n  top-level call. The detector is **not** modified.\n\nEach single-ticket public entry point calls\n`emit_cross_session_warning(ticket_id, repo_root=repo_root)` **before** returning (and, for\nwrites, before the mutation, so the holder is read pre-mutation — matching CLI/MCP). **No\nreturn type changes.** Functions covered, at their definition sites (public names from\n`src/rebar/__init__.py`):\n\n- Reads — `_lib_reads.py`: `show_ticket`, `deps`.\n- Writes — `_lib_writes.py`: `transition` (`reopen` inherits it via delegation).\n- Mutations — `_lib_mutations.py`: `comment`, `edit_ticket` (public name is `edit_ticket`,\n  not `edit`), `link`, `unlink`, `tag`, `untag`, `archive`.\n- Gates — `_lib_gates.py`: `set_file_impact`, `declare_no_file_impact` (library\n  counterpart of the CLI's `set-file-impact --none`), `clarity_check`, `check_ac`.\n  `quality_check` is **out of scope** — absent from the CLI allowlist, deferred on MCP (S4).\n\n`link`/`unlink` warn for the **primary endpoint `id1`** only, matching CLI (S3)/MCP (S4).\nBulk reads (`list_tickets`, `search`, `ready`, `next_batch`) do **not** warn. `claim` is\nexcluded: it raises `ConcurrencyError` on an `in_progress` ticket before any warning path.\n### Surface layering (single-emit dedup)\n\nThe CLI and MCP surfaces call these same library functions, so a naive library emit doubles\nthe advisory each already carries (CLI stderr `WARN:`; MCP `cross_session_warning` field).\nThe dedup keeps exactly one advisory per operation per surface:\n\n- **CLI** (`src/rebar/_cli/_execute.py`) — `execute()` runs `_maybe_warn_cross_session` (the\n  allowlist single source) **and** the handler dispatch inside\n  `suppress_cross_session_warning()`, so the library `CrossSessionWarning` (including the\n  detector's read during detection) is suppressed; the CLI's `WARN:` line is the only CLI\n  advisory.\n- **MCP** (`src/rebar/mcp_server.py`) — `build_server()` installs a process-wide\n  `filterwarnings(\"ignore\", CrossSessionWarning)`, so the response field is the only MCP\n  advisory in the running server.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_lib_warn.py` (**new**) — `CrossSessionWarning(UserWarning)`, best-effort\n  re-entrancy-guarded `emit_cross_session_warning`, and `suppress_cross_session_warning`.\n- `src/rebar/__init__.py` — re-export `CrossSessionWarning` (import + `__all__`).\n- `src/rebar/_lib_reads.py` — emit in `show_ticket`, `deps`.\n- `src/rebar/_lib_writes.py` — emit in `transition` (before the mutation); `reopen`\n  delegates to it, so it does not emit separately (no double warning).\n- `src/rebar/_lib_mutations.py` — emit in `comment`, `edit_ticket`, `link` (`id1`),\n  `unlink` (`id1`), `tag`, `untag`, `archive` (before the mutation).\n- `src/rebar/_lib_gates.py` — emit in `set_file_impact`, `declare_no_file_impact`,\n  `clarity_check`, `check_ac`. `quality_check` out of scope (see Approach).\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_execute.py` — hold `suppress_cross_session_warning()` across detection +\n  dispatch so the library never doubles the CLI `WARN:` line.\n- `src/rebar/mcp_server.py` — `build_server()` ignores `CrossSessionWarning` process-wide.\n- `docs/reuse-surface.md` — document `rebar.CrossSessionWarning`.\n- `tests/unit/test_cross_session_lib.py` (**new**) — the library-surface oracle.\n- `tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json` — refresh for the new `CrossSessionWarning` export.\n- `tests/unit/test_fold_orphan_laundering.py` — exclude the reducer `.cache.json` dotfile\n  from event-file enumeration (library mutations now reduce for the holder pre-check, which\n  persists the cache — matches `graph/_cache.py` / `reconcile_check.py`).\n\n## Testing\n\nTier: **in-process unit test** with stdlib `warnings` capture (`pytest.warns` /\n`catch_warnings(record=True)`). Real temporary tracker; acting session via `REBAR_SESSION_ID`\n(monkeypatch). Claim as holder A, then act as B.\n\n- B vs A-held: `show_ticket` and `comment` each emit one warning naming A; write applies.\n- Write + two-endpoint: `transition` and `link` (holder A on `id1`) each emit one for `id1`.\n- Negative control (same session A): none. Bulk (`list_tickets`/`ready` as B): none.\n- Unset `REBAR_SESSION_ID`: none. Category is `isinstance(..., CrossSessionWarning)`.\n- Re-entrancy: exactly one per top-level `show_ticket`.\n- Best-effort: monkeypatch `cross_session_warning_for` to raise -> call returns, no warning.\n- Per-site sweep: each instrumented fn emits exactly one warning (0=missed, 2=double);\n  reopen delegates to transition (one, not two). CLI dedup: `test_cross_session_cli.py`\n  asserts one `WARN:` per command. Defect-seeded: negate guard / wrong endpoint -> RED.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `rebar.show_ticket(<id>)` and `rebar.comment(<id>, ...)`, as B vs an A-held ticket, each\n  emit exactly one `rebar.CrossSessionWarning` naming holder `A` (`pytest.warns` under\n  `make test`); the `comment` write still applies.\n- [x] `rebar.transition(<id>, \"in_progress\", \"closed\")` and `rebar.link(<id1>, <id2>, ...)`\n  (endpoint `id1`), as B vs A-held `id1`, each emit one `CrossSessionWarning` naming `A`.\n- [x] Same-session A negative control emits none (`catch_warnings(record=True)`).\n- [x] `rebar.list_tickets()` and `rebar.ready()` as B emit none for A's `in_progress` ticket.\n- [x] With `REBAR_SESSION_ID` unset, `rebar.show_ticket(<id>)` emits none.\n- [x] The emitted warning `isinstance(..., rebar.CrossSessionWarning)` subclassing\n  `UserWarning`.\n- [x] Exactly one `CrossSessionWarning` per top-level `rebar.show_ticket(<id>)` despite the\n  detector's internal read (recorded count for that category is 1).\n- [x] Best-effort: when `cross_session_warning_for` raises, the library call returns normally\n  and emits no `CrossSessionWarning` (monkeypatch-to-raise).\n- [x] Single-emit dedup: a warning CLI command (e.g. `link`) writes exactly one `WARN:` line,\n  not doubled by the library channel (`test_cross_session_cli.py` `count(...) == 1`).\n- [x] `docs/reuse-surface.md` documents `rebar.CrossSessionWarning`\n  (`grep -n \"CrossSessionWarning\" docs/reuse-surface.md` matches).","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_lib_warn.py","reason":"new module: CrossSessionWarning(UserWarning), best-effort emit_cross_session_warning, suppress_cross_session_warning context manager"},{"path":"src/rebar/__init__.py","reason":"re-export CrossSessionWarning (import + __all__)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_lib_reads.py","reason":"emit CrossSessionWarning from show_ticket and deps"},{"path":"src/rebar/_lib_writes.py","reason":"emit CrossSessionWarning from transition before the mutation; reopen delegates to transition so it does not emit separately (avoids double warning)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_lib_mutations.py","reason":"emit from comment, edit_ticket, link (id1), unlink (id1), tag, untag, archive before the mutation"},{"path":"src/rebar/_lib_gates.py","reason":"emit from set_file_impact, declare_no_file_impact, clarity_check, check_ac (quality_check excluded)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_execute.py","reason":"hold suppress_cross_session_warning() across detection+dispatch so the library channel does not double the CLI WARN line"},{"path":"src/rebar/mcp_server.py","reason":"build_server() ignores CrossSessionWarning process-wide so the library channel does not double the MCP response field"},{"path":"docs/reuse-surface.md","reason":"document rebar.CrossSessionWarning and single-ticket library emission (bulk reads excluded)"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_cross_session_lib.py","reason":"new library-surface oracle: warns, silence controls, re-entrancy, best-effort, per-site single-emit sweep, reopen single-emit, MCP build_server suppression"},{"path":"tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json","reason":"refresh public-API baseline for the new rebar.CrossSessionWarning export (gen_api_surface --update)"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_fold_orphan_laundering.py","reason":"exclude the reducer .cache.json dotfile from event-file enumeration; library mutations now reduce (holder pre-check) which persists the cache, matching graph/_cache.py and reconcile_check.py conventions"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/cross_session.py","reason":"Reorder cross_session_warning_for to read the config toggle + acting session BEFORE the show_ticket reduce, short-circuiting (and skipping the reduce/cache write) when the feature is disabled — addresses the standing performance advisory."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","0804-9a6b-9182-42c9"],["parent","1aca-695f-a0a4-4236"],["relates_to","3c0d-802b-e17c-4b91"],["relates_to","53b7-951c-df4b-4e36"],["relates_to","72b9-9a83-d4d5-4ea3"],["relates_to","954a-6596-6de9-47a3"],["relates_to","dab7-cfa3-a860-4678"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"1aca-695f-a0a4-4236","parent_status_uuid":"1dd24ce6-cab0-41ef-bab8-df23d9e451ef","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"3d8a-5a5d-8773-473d","ticket_type":"story","title":"Library: warnings.warn CrossSessionWarning from single-ticket functions","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["02236e5b-8363-473d-9031-cfde75f9393a","929d886f-efde-4b96-921b-a782012146fe","55e48ba2-8a84-4323-a436-fe0da70d22aa","0fdb7a5b-9b1d-457b-bc55-1bc6ad53f832","13b7848e-a3f1-4c12-a942-c190832c2cdc","be3c4789-80ba-4ba2-b2b4-d2df440b9764","85e8fcc8-b12e-4f21-84dc-c30d986abf44","1dd24ce6-cab0-41ef-bab8-df23d9e451ef","e544d6b9-30ab-49b2-aaca-9e10decf3363","d2aad1b4-31e9-4fdf-b961-ccaa539683f8","713aa38d-6325-42dc-aa32-a70ec4eefb65","7e4fb90c-f4cd-4d9a-b5b7-8f93a449e819","c816b428-955a-4934-9e7c-0add424656ae","29819876-2f62-42b7-a54a-e6d90d4063ac","5a327ba8-77d8-4482-9ad0-df1b6fcbdb81","36bb23ed-0dbe-4431-b080-b17b3334a48f","08d2ac68-180a-451a-8b16-b8db1309d84a","b9b9adb4-26c2-41e1-9a5c-7eb55ecd5e30","f4f75336-618d-4b1b-b8f4-1078460487cf","8c5e2aec-e139-45b4-bde1-080234655011"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787909826664948816,"uuid":"f972c040-8e8e-4007-8784-fa0d50979a38"}